# Datasets for project days (06-09): committed directly when small enough
# so students don't need a separate download step. Only exclude a specific
# oversized file here when it actually can't fit in git (e.g. European
# Soccer's database.sqlite is 299 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit) —
# decide per-dataset when that day is built, don't blanket-exclude the
# extension.

# Day 06's SQLite files are generated by running day06_python_sqlite.ipynb
# (migrated live from MySQL) — regenerate rather than commit, same reasoning
# as never committing .env.
Day 06/*.sqlite

# Day 07's NBA dataset is 2.3 GB — far over GitHub's 100 MB limit, so it's the
# one project-day dataset that can't be committed directly. Download it per
# Day 07/day07_reading.html's dataset section instead.
Day 07/*.sqlite

# Day 08's European Soccer dataset is ~299 MB — also over GitHub's 100 MB limit.
# Download it per Day 08/day08_reading.html's dataset section instead.
Day 08/*.sqlite
